<BaseLayout title="How the AI query fanout tool works" canonicalPath="/methodology" alternatePath="/de/methode" description="The exact native OpenAI and Gemini search protocol, output boundary, privacy and hard limits."><header class="page-head"><h1>How the free tool works</h1><div class="page-head-copy"><p>One topic goes in. The API runs web search. We show only the queries and sources that response exposes.</p><p class="meta-line">Native tool 1.0 · OpenAI Responses + Gemini Interactions · owner Matthias Ramahi</p></div></header><div class="document-layout"><aside class="document-aside"><dl><div><dt>Primary mode</dt><dd>Native fanout</dd></div><div><dt>Providers</dt><dd>OpenAI + Gemini</dd></div><div><dt>Output</dt><dd>0–8 query strings</dd></div><div><dt>Time limit</dt><dd>20 seconds</dd></div></dl></aside><article class="document-body"><h2>A real API search run, not a browser capture.</h2><p class="document-intro">Native Fanout observes search actions exposed by a direct provider API under one fixed, published protocol. It does not inspect chatgpt.com, gemini.google.com, browser network traffic, system prompts, private retrieval traces or chain of thought.</p><ol class="controls">{steps.map(([title,copy],index)=><li><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,"0")}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></div></li>)}</ol><section><h2>What “native” proves</h2><p>It proves that a specific API run exposed those query strings and citations at that time. It does not prove that a consumer chat product would produce the same fanout, that the source is correct, or that the query has measurable demand.</p></section><section><h2>How to use it for SEO</h2><p>Group observed queries by user job. Add a section when an existing page can answer the job well. Create a new URL only when audience, intent, evidence and next step are genuinely distinct. Never turn every variation into a page automatically.</p></section><section><h2>Responsibility</h2><p>Matthias Ramahi owns protocol versions, corrections, reviewer status and the monthly cost envelope. This tool is not an independent provider benchmark.</p></section></article></div></BaseLayout>
